/-!
# Tensor Pauli record instruments and circuits

This module constructs the tensor Pauli measurement Kraus family, its instrument, and the
corresponding finite record law. Completeness and effect identities establish the Born
probabilities, while summing over signs shows that every choice of measurement axes has mass
`1/3^n`.

Single-wire gates and basis measurements assemble an explicit local observed circuit. Its `2^n`
leaves correspond bijectively to sign records, realize the unweighted Pauli projectors, and
carry exact gate, measurement, and query counts. See [HuangKuengPreskill2020] for background.

## Main statements

* `tensor_pauli_kraus_complete`: reindexing, completeness, and instrument branches.
* `tensor_pauli_actual_local_program`: circuit correctness, leaf indexing, and resources.
* `tensor_pauli_born_record_law`: the record law from instrument and circuit semantics.

## References

* [Huang, Kueng, and Preskill, 2020][HuangKuengPreskill2020]
-/

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

